# SOC Log Analysis Lab

## Overview

This project simulates a beginner SOC (Security Operations Center) environment focused on log analysis and threat detection.

The goal of this lab was to practice:
- Security monitoring
- Log analysis
- Basic threat detection
- SIEM workflows
- Incident investigation concepts

---

## Lab Environment

### Virtual Machines
- Windows 11 VM
- Kali Linux VM

### Tools Used
- Splunk
- Sysmon
- Windows Event Viewer
- VirtualBox

---

## Objectives

- Generate Windows security logs
- Simulate failed login attempts
- Monitor PowerShell execution
- Analyze events using Splunk queries
- Create basic detection rules

---

## Simulated Attacks

### Failed Login Brute Force
Generated multiple failed login attempts to observe Windows Event ID 4625 logs.

### Suspicious PowerShell Activity
Executed PowerShell commands to monitor process creation and Sysmon logging.

---

## Detection Examples

### Failed Login Detection
```spl
index=main EventCode=4625
| stats count by Account_Name, Source_Network_Address
```

### PowerShell Process Detection
```spl
index=main powershell.exe
```

